      "writtenOn": "2024-09-12T17:15:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I might be wrong, but I think these need to be in the other order.\n\nConsider:\n```\ninv. A writes to storage buffer variable x\nstorageBarrier()\ninv. B reads from storage buffer variable x\n```\nWe\u0027d expect `B` to read the value that was written by `A`. With the barriers the way round you have them now, there is no guarantee that `A` will have finished flushing its write with the `memoryBarrierBuffer()` call before `B` gets to the read, because `memoryBarrierBuffer` is not an execution barrier.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 144,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 145,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "f17bb1e9c78a465cb5a0bfcdde55fed83caf6475",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
